{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"15a1b932-989f-4655-aec2-7dfe871ac647","status":"SUCCESS","response":"The integration issues with Intervals.icu have been diagnosed, resolved, and documented in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-FaY3ke/ANSWER.md).\n\n### Summary of Causes \u0026 Fixes\n\n1. **Connect button returned `401 Unauthorized` for all athletes**:\n   - **Cause**: The \"Connect Intervals.icu\" button was implemented as an HTML anchor `\u003ca href=\"/api/intervals/auth/init\"\u003e`. Standard document navigation does not send custom headers like `Authorization: Bearer \u003ctoken\u003e`, which tricoach stores in `localStorage`. Consequently, `require_user()` failed with 401.\n   - **Fix**: In [`static/app.js`](file:///tmp/h-FaY3ke/static/app.js), wired the button click handler to request `/api/intervals/auth/init` via the authenticated `api()` fetch wrapper. Updated [`server.py`](file:///tmp/h-FaY3ke/server.py) so `/api/intervals/auth/init` returns JSON `{ \"url\": target }` for fetch requests, directing the browser to Intervals via `window.location.href`.\n\n2. **OAuth consent returned `400 Bad Request: {\"error\": \"invalid_request\"}`**:\n   - **Cause**: Intervals.icu rejects authorization requests with redundant scopes in the same domain because `:WRITE` automatically includes `:READ` access. Requesting both `ACTIVITY:READ,ACTIVITY:WRITE` and `CALENDAR:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE` triggered duplicate scope rejections.\n   - **Fix**: In [`config.py`](file:///tmp/h-FaY3ke/config.py), updated `SCOPES` to `\"ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE\"`.\n\n3. **Active connections marked \"expired, reconnect\" after one hour**:\n   - **Cause**: Intervals.icu OAuth access tokens are perpetual until manually revoked and omit `expires_in` and `refresh_token`. In `server.py`, `store_connection()` defaulted missing token lifetimes to `DEFAULT_TOKEN_TTL = 3600`, and `refresh_tokens()` subsequently marked the connection as `\"expired, reconnect\"` when the 1-hour timer elapsed with no refresh token present.\n   - **Fix**: In [`server.py`](file:///tmp/h-FaY3ke/server.py), updated `store_connection()` and `refresh_tokens()` so connections without an explicit provider `expires_in` are treated as non-expiring (`expires_at = None`), preventing premature background expiration.\n","duration_seconds":257.009467,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":189609,"output_tokens":6737,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":1929917,"total_tokens":196346}}}
